  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that\r\n$$\r\nR=\\frac{V^{2}}{P}\r\n$$\r\nGiven $\\quad V=200 \\mathrm{V}, P=40 \\mathrm{W}$\r\nand $\\quad V=100 \\mathrm{V}$\r\nHence, $\\quad R=\\frac{V^{2}}{P}=\\frac{200 \\times 200}{50}$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nP=\\frac{V^{2}}{R}=\\frac{100 \\times 100 \\times 50}{200 \\times 200} \\\\\r\nP^{\\prime}=12.5 \\mathrm{W}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
